{"why":
 "Forbid-only: an empty policy set allows everything, so a loader that finds fewer ids than this has a silent permit, not a partial policy. `ids` are the same ids the Rego bundle's `failed_checks` set and the CEL bundle's checks use — one `CheckId.forLeaf`, so the join key cannot drift. `assembly_tiers` names the one extra `forbid` per tier, annotated `@assembly` and carrying no `@id` because it is not a reason leaf: it fires when a tier's inputs were incomplete and no other tier carried the call, which the renderer explains from `call_guards`. A loader must find one policy per id here AND one per assembly tier.",
